<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Siegebreaker (VFEPirates.WarcasketDef,
    ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase") at VFEP commit e237aba,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml. Everything not listed under "Tuning" below is
    still a verbatim Siegebreaker copy (placeholder, per TODOs.md). The apparel tags
    follow the armor's header.

    Tuning: costList Plasteel 70 (Siegebreaker 60) follows the armor's Plasteel rise to 180 at
    the shoulder-to-armor ratio the 10th-gen sets use, roughly 0.4 (Siegebreaker 60/145,
    Guardian 80/200, Controller 60/150, Sarcophagus 60/145, Brute 60/160): 0.4 x 180 = 72,
    rounded to the 10-plasteel steps VFEP's costLists use. No spacer components, like the
    Siegebreaker, Guardian and Sarcophagus shoulders. ArmorRating_Blunt 1.5 is the Brute and
    Guardian shoulders' value; see the armor's header for the set-wide close-combat plating
    rationale.

    Abilities, the breaching arms:
    - SCWC_BreachPower +0.5: the armor's Breach Jump landing deals 900 to a wall cell with these
      on (600 without), enough for plasteel and uranium walls. Structures only; pawn damage is
      unchanged. See 1.6/Defs/StatDefs/BreachPower.xml.
    - equippedStatFactors MeleeHitChance x1.2 and MeleeDodgeChance x1.2 through VEF's
      ApparelExtension: Shock's shoulders' numbers, the only VFEP precedent for the pair, merged
      with the base's extension the way VFEP's own sets do it.
    - No jump-range contribution: a space-centric piece, and the range lives on the armor. No
      EnergyShieldRechargeRate offset either (Siegebreaker's is +1): VEF's CompShieldBubble
      reads that stat off the apparel, never the pawn, so the offset would never reach the
      shield (dead XML in VFEP too).
    - costList GravlitePanel 10 under Odyssey; see the armor's header for the split.

    SOS2/Universum: our 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml deliberately leaves shoulder pads alone,
    mirroring VFEP's own patch, which only touches armor and helmets.

    Vanilla Gravship Expanded: our VGE1 vacuum patch (see the armor's header) leaves the
    shoulders' 0.1 alone, exactly as VGE1 leaves VFEP's.

    Art: Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerShoulders (+
    _north/_east/_south), 256x256 RGBA under the root Textures/ folder, mirroring VFEP's own
    warcasket layout.

    Draw order: dataNorth offset y 0.05 (base 0.2) and dataSouth offset y 0.014 (base 0.02). A
    worn apparel node's altitude is its drawData offset's y (added verbatim by
    PawnRenderTree.TryGetMatrix) plus PawnRenderUtility.AltitudeForLayer(layer), 0.000366 per
    layer unit, where the layer is the parent node's base (ApparelBody 20, ApparelHead 70) plus
    the piece's index among that parent's apparel; the y offsets VFEP's bases carry are what
    actually order the pieces. Both changes only ever move this piece, so every helmet and
    armor, ours or VFEP's, keeps its VFEP altitude and the foundry's mix-and-match stays
    consistent; not by lifting our helmet instead, since that then sat over other sets'
    pauldrons in game.

    - North: the base's 0.2 puts the pauldrons over the shell (0.107). This art wants the
      shell's back frame over the pauldron inner edges, so 0.05 lands them at about 0.058: under
      the shell, still above the bodysuit (VEF's secondaryApparelGraphics feeds
      VFEP_Warcasket_Bodysuit through vanilla ProcessApparel with that def's own null drawData,
      so it stays near 0.008 in every facing and never moves with the shell), the helmet (0.026,
      the head chain adds no y of its own) and pack-layer apparel (layer 93, 0.034).
    - South: the base's 0.02 lands at 0.027 to 0.028 (index 0 to 3), just over the helmets at
      0.001 + 70 x 0.000366 = 0.027. The art wants the helmet over the pauldron inner edges, so
      0.014 lands them at 0.021 to 0.022: at least 0.004 under any helmet and 0.003 over the
      shell's 0.017 to 0.018, above post-apparel wounds (layer 30, 0.011) and firefoam (40,
      0.015). Hair and beard (62 and 60, about 0.022) would draw over them if a wearer had no
      helmet hiding the head, which is what hair does over shoulders anyway.

    East/west inherit the base's 0.02. Only the facings that change are listed: XmlInheritance
    merges same-named elements recursively, so the other RotationalData entries come through
    from VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>SCWC_WarcasketShoulders_Shipcracker</defName>
    <label>shipcracker warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Placeholder shipcracker warcasket pauldrons. Stats are an untuned copy of the siegebreaker warcasket shoulders for now.</shortDescription>
    <description>Placeholder description for the shipcracker warcasket pauldrons. It is a stand-in for later tuning, not lore.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerShoulders</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>20</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>22</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>22</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.1</VacuumResistance>
      <SCWC_BreachPower>0.5</SCWC_BreachPower>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <Plasteel>70</Plasteel>
      <GravlitePanel MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">10</GravlitePanel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <!-- Under the shell facing north and under the helmet facing south; see
           "Draw order" in the header. -->
      <drawData>
        <dataNorth><offset>(0, 0.05, 0)</offset></dataNorth>
        <dataSouth><offset>(0, 0.014, 0)</offset></dataSouth>
      </drawData>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <!-- Reusing WarcasketVeteran puts this set on every Junker/Mercenary
             veteran-tier pawnkind (and Odyssey's salvager pawnkind); see
             TODOs.md open question.
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        -->
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <!-- priority: makes this entry the survivor when VEF merges it with the one
             VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase carries; see the armor def's header. -->
        <priority>1</priority>
        <equippedStatFactors>
          <MeleeHitChance>1.2</MeleeHitChance>
          <MeleeDodgeChance>1.2</MeleeDodgeChance>
        </equippedStatFactors>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
